      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Emergency response architects executed a precision load-reduction design, a carefully crafted control action to prevent a critical 230-kilovolt transmission line from overloading. This measure was a direct response to a massive 950-megawatt power deficit, showcasing a form of crisis management where operational protocols are sculpted under extreme pressure to maintain grid stability.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
        "fragments": [
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "how-2",
        "center_kind": "how",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 1
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "A generator experienced a system failure, a grid incident that marked the beginning of the crisis. This equipment failure, alongside seasonal heat driving demand into a thin operating margin, set the stage for the subsequent emergency measures. The event underscores how a single point of failure in energy infrastructure can cascade, forcing the entire system to respond.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
        "fragments": [
